  "deprecation": {
    "reason": "Superseded by CodeBlock (2026-10-25, react 0.1.38). CodeBlockWindow drew macOS window chrome (traffic-light dots, centred title, text Copy button) around a Shiki tree and had one layout switch (context=\"article\"). CodeBlock keeps what worked (Flight-lazy unwrapping before introspecting server children, copy with an execCommand fallback, the Lenis wheel opt-out for scrollable bodies, translated region label) and adds a filename header or floating copy column, line numbers, highlighted/added/removed rows with signs, a terminal theme, wrap and maxHeight, and runtime highlighting for code strings. Migrated consumers: ArticlePageTemplate MDX figures, /dev/code-window."
